The function recover_json_object, when given a reply containing a fenced JSON object whose string value includes triple backticks, truncates the fenced content at the first triple backticks and therefore fails to score the fenced object, instead returning the last top-level object outside the fence, making the reply indistinguishable from one without a fence; this is asserted to be incorrect according to the documented rule that the last object inside a code fence should be scored when any fence holds one.